## 4. GLBP (Gateway Load Balancing Protocol)

GLBP is a Cisco proprietary FHRP protocol. It provides both Gateway Redundancy and Load Balancing.

Unlike HSRP and VRRP, where normally one Router forwards traffic, GLBP allows multiple Routers to forward traffic simultaneously.

**How Does It Work?**

- AVG (Active Virtual Gateway): Manages the Virtual Gateway.
- AVF (Active Virtual Forwarder): Forwards Client traffic.
- Multiple Routers share the traffic load.
- If one Router fails, another Router can continue forwarding traffic.

